Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  Report Status  Signed  Type  Surgical Pathology  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS   A  Right breast  simple mastectomy    Focal atypical ductal hyperplasia  probably in an intraductal papilloma   Fibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia   Excision site with fibrosis   B  Left breast  simple mastectomy    Fibrocystic changes   NOTE  No residual carcinoma is seen in specimen A   Final Diagnosis by  Richard J  Sampson  M D   Clinical diagnosis   history   Right breast carcinoma  had neoadjuvant chemo  left breast prophylactic  Tissue Designation   A Breast  simple mastectomy   right  B Breast  simple mastectomy   left  Gross description   The specimen is received in two containers   Specimen A labeled is  right breast   The specimen has an ellipse of skin  centrally placed  It includes only the areola which is 3 x 2 5cm  A stitch  is present  said to be 12 o clock  The specimen is entirely inked  Sections  are taken across the breast from the 12 o clock to the 6 o clock end  The  specimen weighs 305 grams  Near the 6 o clock end of the specimen in the mid  portion is an area of induration  Sections are taken from 12 to 6 o clock  labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The nipple is labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   10X   Specimen B labeled  left breast  consists of a breast which weighs 344 grams  and has a stitch present at 6 o clock  It measures overall 16 x 13 x 1cm  A  nipple is present which is not inverted and which has an areolar diameter of 3  x 2cm  No other skin is present on the specimen  The specimen is about half  composed of adipose tissue and the rest  fibroglandular tissue with a few small  cysts but no tumors or other lesions  The nipple is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the  remainder is from random breast tissue from 6 to 12 o clock  8X   Dictated by  RJS____ signature on file ____RICHARD SAMPSON  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final    report_end  , no_Medullary.
