ctivity for progesterone receptor in both the low grade and  intermediate grade CIS are unusual and suggest that both the low grade and the  intermediate grade CIS may not behave as usual lobular in situ neoplasia   Slides also seen by Dr  Susan Lester  who concurs   CLINICAL DATA   History  53 year old female with R breast cancer in situ carcinoma with mixed  ductal and lobular features   Operation  R breast wire localized partial mastectomy   Operative Findings  Not provided   Clinical Diagnosis  R breast DCIS   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  R breast tissue with wire  standard in please don t apply extra ink to  crevis sic  on anterior margin    RADIOLOGY   Specimen has wire and clip  Dr  BAL called SR   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  and unit  number  and   1  Right breast tissue with wire   and consists of a REMOVED_DATE  medial  to lateral  x REMOVED_DATE  inferior to superior  x REMOVED_DATE  anterior to posterior cm  breast biopsy with a localization wire in place  which enters the specimen at  the lateral anterior border  An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates  a clip along the superior medial margins  The specimen is inked per pathology  protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue   superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  The medial and  lateral segments are removed and submitted as perpendicular sections  and the  remainder of the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan white cut  surface with a focal area of hemorrhage  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm and a tan brown area of firmness  measuring 1 0cm x 0 5cm along the  superior posterior border  The specimen is entirely submitted for analysis   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial segment  perpendicular sections  2 frags per cassette  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral segment  perpendicular sections  multi frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  