rom the posterior margin  This area is in the region of two of the needle localization wires  Also noted in the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm region denoted by two needle localization wires in the medial portion of the specimen which show a focally calcified and fibrotic region  Also within this region  there are focal small  round  tan yellow areas which appear to represent caseous necrosis  There is no distinct mass identified  The intervening breast parenchyma is tan white  focally fibrous  and predominant fibrofatty  Photographs of the specimen have been taken  Representative sections are submitted as per section code  Section Code  A D  0 9cm nodule in lateral breast  E G  Intervening unremarkable appearing breast parenchyma  H P  Calcifications denoted by medial localization wires  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  and  primary sentinel node  150   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm node  In addition  a smaller firm region of possibly hemorrhagic fat is noted in the specimen  The largest lymph node is bisected to reveal a tan white and focally fatty cut surface with scattered punctate red foci  This largest bisected node is entirely submitted into cassette Q  the remainder fibrofatty tissue and smaller nodular region are submitted into cassette R  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  and  secondary sentinel node  80   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggegrate of yellow fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node  The lymph node and attached fibrofatty tissue are entirely submitted into cassette S  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  and  tertiary sentinel node  79   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm lymph node with a fibrofatty and focally tan pink cut surface  The bisected node is entirely submitted into cassette T and U and the remainder of the fibrofatty tissue is entirely submitted into cassette V  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE LEFT PRIMARY AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE LEFT SECONDARY AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISIO PART D  LYMPH NODE LEFT TERTIARY AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISION , no_Medullary.
