Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Amend Addenda  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast core needle biopsy  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  ELISABETH P FROST M D   CASE  BS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME              Addended Report              Resident  Mariana A  Stoleru  M D   Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST  9 G MRI GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES   UPPER OUTER  REMOVED_DATE CM AREA OF SLIGHTLY IRREGULAR ENHANCEMENT   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  moderately differentiated  modified Bloom   Richardson grade II III   measuring at least 0 4cm in size   No definite lymphovascular invasion is seen   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present   Note  The LCIS has a slightly higher nuclear grade than is typical and  there is single cell necrosis   Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor  progesterone  receptor  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu will be performed and reported in an addendum   LOWER OUTER  1 CM AREA OF NON MASS FORMING ENHANCEMENT   Columnar cell change with apocrine metaplasia and calcifications   Atypical lobular hyperplasia   CLINICAL DATA   HISTORY  54 year old female with history of ADH and LCIS on prior biopsies   with 2 focally enhancing areas in left breast   BREAST IMAGING FINDING   1  Site  1  upper outer  0 4cm  focal enhancement  slightly spiculated   2  Site  2  lower outer  1cm  focal and non mass forming   The two sites are 4cm apart   LOCATION   1  Left  upper outer  2  Left  lower outer  TYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY   1  9G MRI Vacuum assisted  2  9G MRI Vacuum assisted  TISSUE SUBMITTED   2  9G MRI Vacuum assisted A 1    Green top white bottom  B 2    Blue top  white bottom  GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received in formalin  in two parts  each labeled with the  patient s name  unit number   Part A  labeled  left breast site  1   consists of three white cassettes with  green lids containing multiple cylindrical fibrofatty focally hemorrhagic soft  tissues  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate   which are submitted in toto   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contents of white cassettes with green lids  multi frags in each   ESS   Part B  labeled  left breast site  2   contains four white cassettes with blue  lids with multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues  3 0  x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate   which are submitted in toto   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contents of white cassettes with blue lid  multi frags in each   ESS   CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    JC ag  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Friday  February 13   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 17 27PM  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  2 19 09    Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for invasive carcinoma  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NEGATIVE  1    Note  Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for  progesterone receptors   Immunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following  criteria   Hormone receptor analysis   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low   0      10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  of nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not  yet been determined    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu analysis   Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but  only a portion of the membrane is positive   Equivocal  2   Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells   Positive  3   Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells   Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   External controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity   Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational  use only   Addendum  1 by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on Thursday  February 19   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07 44 28PM  SURGICAL ADDENDUM   An immunoperoxidase study for e cadherin is performed on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although  the invasive carcinoma has lobular morphology  the carcinoma is moderately  immunoreactive  Therefore  this is an unusual lobular carcinoma with  e cadherin expression  Some of the in situ carcinoma is also e cadherin  positive  Other cells have weak or absent expression  Final classification of  both components should be made on the excisional specimen   Addendum  2 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Wednesday  REMOVED_MONTH 22   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07 24 18PM   report_end  , no_Medullary.
