Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  MEHRA GOLSHAN M D   CASE  BS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Resident  Christian J  Davidson  M D   Pathologist  Jane E  Brock  M B   B S   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A  RIGHT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   Columnar cell change  intraductal papilloma  apocrine metaplasia  and small  cysts  with scattered microcalcifications  see NOTE   The margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis   NOTE  The patient is s p a core needle biopsy for calcifications which revealed  ALH and calcifications associated with benign epithelium  this was the  diagnosis on review at BWH see  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   but reported as ADH   ALH on  initial outside hospital pathology review   Per Radiology report available in  LMR  BWH  06 17 09   residual calcifications are not present at the site of  biopsy and the clip marking the presence of a biopsy site was noted to be 4cm  inferior to the site of biopsied calcifications  In this current excision which  aimed to re excise the prior biopsy site  but not the clip   no biopsy site  changes are seen   CLINICAL DATA   History  48 year old female with right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia  after image guide core biopsy   Operation  Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy   Operative Findings  Not provided   Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy  short suture superior  long  suture lateral   mammo   RADIOLOGY   The area of prior biopsy and intact wire are in the specimen   Called to Dr  Golshan in OR by Dr  Yeh  12 05 pm   GROSS DESCRIPTION   This case consists of one part  and is received fresh and clearly labeled with  the patient s name and medical record number   Specimen A  labeled   1  Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy  short  suture superior  long suture lateral mammo   and consists of one wire  localized breast excisional biopsy measuring 2 5cm superior to inferior  REMOVED_DATE  cm medial to lateral  and 1 6cm anterior to posterior  A short suture  designates the superior margin and a long suture designates the lateral margin   per the surgeon   A localization wire enters at the superior margin and exits  at the inferior margin  A radiograph received with the specimen shows that the  thickened area of wire is in a radiodense  fibrous  region of the specimen   Sectioning through the specimen reveals 70  fibrous and 30  adipose tissue   The fibrous tissue abuts all margins  No discrete masses or lesions are noted   The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins   posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow   medial orange  The entire specimen is submitted for histologic analysis   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire specimen sectioned superior to inferior  with superior  perpendicular in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and inferior perpendicular in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    multi frags total  ESS   CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    chd elw  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Jane E  Brock M B   B S   Ph D   Electronically signed on  Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 23   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 51 13PM   report_end  , no_Medullary.
 REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAYNTER MARTHA  P  49 F  REG REF 03 02    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC FINN LEONARD M  M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  03 02 05  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  5mm  cluster of indeterminate calcifications  left posterior upper outer quadrant    fibrocystic changes vs ductal carcinoma in situ Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereotactic loc reduced SVC  left breast calcifications  and consists of two cassettes  The first  which is purple in color and designated on the specimen requisition to be the upper outer quadrant with calcifications  consists of three firm  yellow  glistening needle biopsies measuring 2cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter to 3cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter  3X all  labeled 1  The second  which is yellow in color and designated on the specimen requisition to be the remainder of the tissue  consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  aggregate of yellowish red  firm needle biopsies measuring 0 3cm  in diameter each  2 agg  all  labeled REMOVED_DATE Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DIAGNOSIS  Left breast  posterior upper outer quadrant  needle core biopsies  Microcalcifications identified and associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia  columnar type  see note   Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  This case was sent to dr  Fritz Koerner at Massachusetts General Hospital  He concurs and adds  The tissue in the background of this core biopsy specimen shows stromal atrophy  You have marked a small duct and several terminal duct lobular units distended by a population of atypical ductal cells  They appear enlarged and they possess slightly enlarged  smoothly contoured  oval or round nuclei  homogeneous chromatin  inconspicuous nucleoli  and modest amounts of eosinophilic  apical cytoplasm  Most of the cells grow in a single  sometimes crowded or pseudostratified layer  however  those in a few foci seem to show genuine stratification and the formation of miniature micropapillary tufts  The presence of these cytological alterations identifies the cells as atypical  and the crowding and stratification of the cells imply a significant degree of proliferation of the atypical population  Because of these findings  I would not hesitate to make the diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar cell type  I share your concerns about the frequent lack of significant findings in specimens excised because of a diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia  Approximately sixty percent of our cases showing atypical columnar cell hyperplasia on a core biopsy specimen fall into this category  Perhaps we will learn criteria that will allow us to reduce this percentage  but I would not back away from the diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia in the case at hand   Final Diagnosis by  Nicole A  Mihok  M D  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ Notes  REMOVED_DATE  Received all 9 slides and report from Dr Winer via mail  NAM td  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE  Sent all nine slides to Dr  Eric Winer   DFCI via courier at the req of Leanna NWH Breast Center  jam   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    617  REMOVED_DATE  Dr Winer  REMOVED_DATE  Rec d all nine slides from Dr  Koerner  dg CR REMOVED_DATE  Second report faxed from MGH  jam REMOVED_DATE  Rec d path report from Dr  Koerner via fax  dg REMOVED_DATE  Sent nine slides  1 1L 3L  2 1L 3L and 3 1L 3L  to Dr  Frederick Koerner   MGH via courier for opinion NAM jam  CO   617  REMOVED_DATE Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT CORCCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Left breast  NO Needle  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Left breast  NO Posterior BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Atypical hyperp Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCOPIES TO  FINN LEONARD M  M D  65 WALNUT STREET WELLESLEY  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   781 235  REMOVED_CASE_ID  SELLAND DONNA LEE M D  NEWTON WELLESLEY RADIOLOGY NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 243  REMOVED_CASE_ID MARKERS  Breast Disease Related  Presented at Breast CA Conf   Consult Case Out  Consult Out 2  Consult Return 2  Kodachromes in file Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT CORCPROCEDURES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   03 03 05  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJTISSUES  Breast  needle biopsy   left Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJFinal  SAMPSON RICHARD J MD   REMOVED_DATE  03 03 05  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD SAMR MIHOK NICOLE MD        REMOVED_DATE  03 04 05  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD MIHN                                                                                              , no_Medullary.
