Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  Report Status  Signed  Type  Surgical Pathology  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS   Right breast  excision   Fibroadenoma   Fibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia  sclerosing adenosis and  microcalcifications   Slight atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar type  single microscopic focus   see note    NOTE  The slides were sent in consultation to Dr  Frederick C  Koerner at  Massachusetts General Hospital who concurs and states the following in  his consultation letter    The tissue in the background of this excision specimen shows  fibrocystic changes and a small focus of adenosis  I agree that the  nodule in question represents a fibroadenoma  The epithelium within it  looks stratified in several areas  but I attribute most of this  appearance to tangential sectioning  One small region on slide  9    which I dotted  probably does display genuine ductal hyperplasia  which  looks similar to the foci of ductal hyperplasia in the surrounding  tissue  I would not regard either focus as atypical  The region of  slide  7  that caught your attention looks a bit different  these  proliferative cells have columnar shapes  atypical nuclei  and abundant  apical cytoplasm  Because of these findings  I would classify this tiny  focus as atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar cell type  The degree  of proliferation strikes me as minimal  though  and the atypicality as  subtle  I do not think that such a minuscule lesion would require  further investigation or treatment unless the clinical details of the  case suggest otherwise    Final Diagnosis by  Daniel D  Koelliker  M D   Clinical diagnosis   history   Right breast mass  Tissue Designation   Breast  excision  without margins    right  Gross description   The specimen is received in formalin  labeled  right breast mass  and consists  of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm  aggregate of multiple irregular portions of fibroadipose  tissue  Each of the portions is primarily rubbery  pink and white tan fibrous  tissue with a small amount of surrounding adipose tissue  No grossly  suspicious areas are seen  The entire specimen is sectioned  Focally  there  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  bulging  pink tan area  The entire specimen is  submitted in REMOVED_DATE 9 agg  all   Dictated by  DDK____ signature on file ____MICHAEL J  ROSS  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final   ____ signature on file ____DANIEL D  KOELLIKER  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final    report_end  , no_Medullary.
